artifact.self_contained_problem:
Let $(M,g)$ be a closed (compact, without boundary) connected smooth pseudo-Riemannian manifold. Suppose there exists a $(1,1)$-tensor field $L$ on $M$ (equivalently, a smooth field of endomorphisms $L:TM\to TM$) such that:
(i) $L\not\equiv 0$;
(ii) $L$ is $g$-self-adjoint, i.e. $g(LX,Y)=g(X,LY)$ for all vector fields $X,Y$;
(iii) $L$ is parallel with respect to the Levi-Civita connection $\nabla$ of $g$, i.e. $\nabla L=0$;
(iv) $L$ is nilpotent, i.e. $L^k=0$ at every point of $M$ for some integer $k\ge 2$.

Question: Do such pairs $(M,g,L)$ exist? More precisely, classify (or determine constraints on) closed pseudo-Riemannian manifolds admitting a non-zero parallel, $g$-self-adjoint, nilpotent $(1,1)$-tensor field. (Note that in the Riemannian signature, any $g$-self-adjoint nilpotent endomorphism must vanish identically, so the question is meaningful only in indefinite signature.)

